.962 .096(Definitions of the arc algorithms.)J
90 477 :M
.734 .073(Both algorithms proceed in sequential steps with a user defined limit of how many steps until)J
90 489 :M
1.286 .129(termination.   Initialize probabilities {p\(n\)} to be equal. At each step, the new training set is)J
90 501 :M
2.276 .228(selected by sampling from the original training set using probabilities {p\(n\)}.  After the)J
90 513 :M
.629 .063(classifier based on this resampled training set is constructed, the {p\(n\)} are updated depending)J
90 525 :M
.841 .084(on the misclassifications up to the present step.    On termination the classifiers are combined)J
90 537 :M
1.507 .151(using weighted \(arc-fs\) or unweighted \(arc-x4\) voting.   The arc-fs algorithm is based on a)J
90 549 :M
-.005(boosting theorem given in Freund and Schapire [1995].  Arc-x4 is an ad hoc invention.)A
90 573 :M
