.596 .06(After a training set T' is selected by sampling from T with probabilities {p\(n\)}, another set T'' is)J
90 458 :M
.325 .033(generated the same way.  T' is used for tree construction, T'' is used as a test set for pruning.  By)J
90 470 :M
1.641 .164(eliminating the need for cross-validation pruning, 50 classification trees can be grown and)J
90 482 :M
.374 .037(pruned in about the same cpu time as it takes for 5 trees grown and pruned using 10-fold cross-)J
90 494 :M
.831 .083(validation.  This is also true for bagging.  Thus, both  arcing and bagging, applied to decision)J
90 506 :M
1.221 .122(trees, grow classifiers relatively fast.   Parallel bagging can be easily implemented but arc is)J
90 518 :M
1.955 .196(essentially sequential.)J
