90 574 :M
1.762 .176( Another complex aspect of arcing  is illustrated in the experiments done to date.  In the)J
90 586 :M
2.591 .259(diabetes data set it gives higher error rate than a single run of CART.   The Freund-)J
90 598 :M
.794 .079(Schapire[1996] and Quinlan[1996] experiments used C4.5, a tree structured program similar to)J
90 610 :M
.18 .018(CART and compared C4.5 to the arc-fs and bagging classifiers based on C4.5.   In 5 of the 39 data)J
90 622 :M
.636 .064(sets examined in the two experiments, the arc-fs test set error was over 20% larger than that of)J
90 634 :M
.775 .078(C4.5.  This did not occur with bagging.    Its not understood why arc-fs causes this infrequent)J
90 646 :M
.599 .06(degeneration in test set error, usually  with smaller data sets.    One conjecture is that this may)J
90 658 :M
1.702 .17(be caused by outliers in the data.   An outlier will be consistently misclssified, so that its)J
90 670 :M
.48 .048(probability of being sampled will continue to increase as the arcing continues.  It will then start)J
90 682 :M
.478 .048(appearing  multiple times in the resampled data sets.  In small data sets, this may be enough to)J
90 694 :M
1.6 .16(warp the classifiers.)J
